xmodel/bd-fix3-quadratic-discriminant-conductor-invariant-hostile-review-opus5-20260830.log:6:Items 1–2 CONFIRMED outright. I reconstructed the Gram determinant from the AL3 table and got `81a²d² − 108a³c − 108bd³ − 27b²c² + 162abcd` — exactly (2.1), and exactly `Disc(Φ)` in the classical convention, so the residual "convention scalar" is **1**, not merely nonzero. Verified on two instances (`(0,1,−1,0)` gives `z³=−1`, disc `−27`; `(0,1,0,1)` gives `−108`), which pins the `−3` in `Tr(zw)`. Degree-four homogeneity and `deg ≤ 8` confirmed. The packet's unnamed "net exponent" is `6−4=2`, agreeing with (1.2).
