xmodel/max12-812-order2-p0-total-rees-j2-certificate-design-grok-20260827.log:30:**Box02 queue (structured Macaulay linear algebra, not Groebner):** A replay of the T-a0 identity (mandatory control), then concurrent B1 `a1^3`, B2 `a1^3(1+rho W)`, and C a T-a0 `W=0` hunt seeded by `Tg15_6 - rho^2 Tg15_4`. B3 (`k` retained) only if B1/B2 miss. Cap: 64 GiB, 1800 s, 8 threads.
xmodel/r5-charge-sheet-draft-grok46-20260831.md:106:So an `F_{109}`-linear matrix of first-order unknowns is the coefficient matrix of `L(Ā,B̄) = x^{108}`, which is a *necessary* reduction of (1.1), not a substitute for (1.1). The nonlinear term `109 N` is invisible over `F_{109}`. Consequently this matrix ring cannot, by itself, be a floor-twelve test: the two-slot family `A_0=y^m`, `B_0=x^{108} y` already solves the reduced equation for every `m≥1` (support gate `117–140`; review claim 3 CONFIRMED).
xmodel/r5-charge-sheet-draft-grok46-20260831.md:118:**Why floor-twelve constrains this choice.** The promoted floor (producer `17–20`; review verdict CONFIRMED at line 7; no-cap firewall `20–22`) is:
xmodel/r5-charge-sheet-draft-grok46-20260831.md:151:Banked two-sided exclusions, both corrections simultaneously, arbitrary finite `x`-degree: `≤2` (quadratic gate `14–19`), `≤3` (cubic `(3.2)` at cubic `316`), `≤4` (quartic `7–10,25–30`). Affine-`y` (both `deg_y ≤1`) is an independent no-go (closed-support Thm 3.1). Floor-twelve, promoted: `max(deg_y A, deg_y B) ≥ 12` (floor-twelve producer `17–20`; review CONFIRMED). One-sided: `deg_y Q = deg_y B ≥ 6` (prime/4 `(1.2)`), strengthening AS-TRI `deg_y B ≥ 2`. AS-TRI licensed compositions kill the two-sided shapes `(deg_y A, deg_y B) = (12,0)` and `(12,1)`.
